          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সুখ — sukh — \"happiness; comfort\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আমার দাদু গ্রামে সুখে আছেন। āmār dādu grāme sukhe āchhen. My grandfather lives happily in the village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সুখে থাকা, to live happily."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সুখ (sukh) is a tatsama, Sanskrit sukha, \"pleasant, easy\" (CDIAL 13451), and so comfort and happiness; সুখী (taught), contented, is the adjective made from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
